\subsection{Full Per-Attack APCER / BPCER / ACER}

Table~\ref{tab:full_per_attack} presents the complete three-metric
breakdown for the three representative methods.
BBDM achieves uniformly low APCER on physical/material attacks
(Artifact, PostMortem) because these textures are maximally far
from the bona fide manifold. Display-based attacks (E-display,
CL) are hardest because their textures partially overlap with
genuine iris patterns.

