% ============================================================
\section{Ablation Studies}
\label{sec:ablation}

\subsection{BBDM: Denoising Steps}

Table~\ref{tab:bbdm_steps} ablates the number of reverse diffusion
steps. Performance improves consistently up to 100 steps, after which
gains plateau. We recommend 100 steps as the operating point,
achieving nearly the same ACER as 200 steps at half the cost.

\begin{table}[!h]
\centering
\caption{BBDM ablation: denoising steps vs.\ PAD metrics
  and inference time per image.}
\label{tab:bbdm_steps}
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.1}
\begin{tabular}{cS[table-format=2.2]S[table-format=2.2]
